<div class="static-page">
  <section class="static-page__intro">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="static-page__subtitle">
      What personal data Tempasi processes, why, for how long, and what
      you can do about it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="static-page__notice">
    <strong>Draft — pending legal review.</strong> This describes what the
    Tempasi code actually does today. Fields in [brackets] are still open
    and must be filled in before Tempasi accepts live payments. It has not
    yet been reviewed by a lawyer.
  </div>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Short version</h2>
    <p>
      We process the data needed to run your account, your orders and the
      templates you list — nothing more. No analytics, no advertising, no
      tracking cookies, no selling of data. Payments are handled by Stripe;
      we never see your card details.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The controller under the GDPR is the operator named in the
      <a href="/impressum">Impressum</a>:<br />
      [Full name], [address], Germany<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:support@tempasi.com">support@tempasi.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Tempasi is not required to appoint a data protection officer.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>What we process and why</h2>

    <h3>Visiting the site</h3>
    <p>
      When you open any page, the web server processes your IP address,
      the requested URL, date and time, browser type (user agent) and the
      referring page. This is technically necessary to deliver the site
      and to detect abuse and attacks. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
      (legitimate interest in a secure, working site). Server logs are
      deleted after [14] days.
    </p>
    <p>
      All fonts, styles and scripts come from Tempasi's own server or
      your device — no request goes to Google Fonts or any other
      third-party CDN.
    </p>

    <h3>Your account</h3>
    <p>
      Email address and password (stored only as a one-way bcrypt hash —
      we can't read it), plus whether your email is verified. We use your
      email for login, account verification, password resets and messages
      about your orders. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (contract).
    </p>

    <h3>Your profile</h3>
    <p>
      Optional details you choose to add: name, display name, avatar,
      about text, location, website, public email and role. If you turn on
      <strong>public profile</strong>, these are shown to other registered
      users in the Community directory, and your display name appears on
      templates you list. If you leave it off, they're only visible to you
      and to Tempasi. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h3>Orders and payments</h3>
    <p>
      What you bought or rented, prices, dates, rental periods, credit
      balance, and the confirmation you gave about the right of
      withdrawal. Payment itself is processed by Stripe (see below):
      Tempasi receives only the payment status and a reference, never your
      card number. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, and Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR
      for records we are legally required to keep.
    </p>

    <h3>Templates and Cases</h3>
    <p>
      If you sell, we store the templates you upload, their descriptions
      and prices, and sales/rental statistics shown in your Analytics. If
      you use Cases, we store the case names and the templates you add to
      them. A client preview link works for anyone who has the link — share
      it only with the client it's meant for, and avoid putting other
      people's personal data into case names. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b)
      GDPR.
    </p>

    <h3>Contacting us</h3>
    <p>
      If you email us, we process your message and email address to answer
      it. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if it relates to your account or an
      order, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      One strictly necessary session cookie (<code>sid</code>) that keeps
      you logged in. No consent is required for it (§ 25(2) TDDDG). Details
      on the <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Live demos</h2>
    <p>
      Template live demos are content created by sellers. They run on a
      separate domain (<code>templates.web-globus.de</code>), isolated from
      your Tempasi account — they can't read your Tempasi session. A demo
      may load its own resources (for example fonts or images from other
      sites), which Tempasi does not control.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      We use these processors, bound by data processing agreements
      (Art. 28 GDPR):
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Hetzner Online GmbH</strong>, Gunzenhausen, Germany —
        server hosting (data centre in Nuremberg, Germany).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd.</strong>, Dublin, Ireland —
        payment processing. Stripe may transfer data to the USA; Stripe,
        Inc. is certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
        Stripe processes some payment data as an independent controller;
        see Stripe's own privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>[Email provider]</strong>, [location] — sending account
        and order emails.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>[Cloudflare, Inc. — only if the domain is proxied through
        Cloudflare; remove if Cloudflare is DNS-only]</strong>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We don't pass your data to anyone else, unless we are legally
      obliged to (for example to tax authorities).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> [14] days.</li>
      <li><strong>Account and profile:</strong> as long as your account exists.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Orders, invoices and payment records:</strong> up to
        10 years, as required by German tax and commercial law (§ 147 AO,
        § 257 HGB), even after your account is deleted.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account yourself under
      <strong>Cabinet → Profile &amp; Security</strong>. This immediately
      disables login and removes your profile and listings from public
      view. Templates other users already bought or rented stay available
      to them. Records we are legally required to keep (see above) are
      retained until that period ends. If you want everything else erased
      completely, email
      <a href="mailto:support@tempasi.com">support@tempasi.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access your data (Art. 15 GDPR), to correct it
      (Art. 16), to have it erased (Art. 17), to restrict processing
      (Art. 18), to data portability (Art. 20) and to object to processing
      based on legitimate interest (Art. 21). To use any of these, email
      <a href="mailto:support@tempasi.com">support@tempasi.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority.
      The one responsible for Tempasi is the Bayerisches Landesamt für
      Datenschutzaufsicht (BayLDA), Promenade 18, 91522 Ansbach, Germany.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Other points</h2>
    <p>
      We don't use automated decision-making or profiling. Providing your
      email and a password is required to create an account; everything in
      your profile is optional.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we change how we process data, we'll update this page and, for
      significant changes, tell registered users by email.
    </p>
    <p><em>Last updated: [date].</em></p>
  </section>
</div>
